# Local run listens on 8080 (set PORT to change it); in Docker Compose the replica is on 8081

### Instruments with their latest price
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/instruments

### Latest price of one instrument
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/instruments/NVDA/price

### Live ticks (Server-Sent Events), at most one per symbol every 500 ms
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/stream/ticks?symbols=AAPL,NVDA&throttleMs=500
Accept: text/event-stream

### Live 5-second candles
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/stream/candles?interval=5s&symbols=BTC-USD
Accept: text/event-stream

### Stored 1-minute candles, latest 30
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/candles/AAPL?interval=1m&limit=30

### Create an alert
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/alerts
Content-Type: application/json

{"symbol": "NVDA", "direction": "ABOVE", "price": 140}

### Alerts that are still active
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/alerts?status=ACTIVE

### Alerts as they fire
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/alerts/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

### WebSocket (use a WebSocket client): ws://localhost:8080/ws/ticks
# then send {"action": "subscribe", "symbols": ["AAPL", "BTC-USD"]}
